domain KshiaiCharacterCreateBoundary:
  description "Bounded investigation of two current offline character-create route failures"

problem P1:
  |
    All original test files must become current and pass without removing cases,
    weakening functional creation or activation, or accepting an unvalidated profile.
    The current structured-character HTTP suite has 13 passing and two failing cases.

evidence E1:
  |
    /tmp/kshiai-character-create-current-failures.tap records13 passes and2 failures.
    uses current V3 attempts for create review confirm and discard routes receives
    404 instead of202 at POST character-drafts/:id/chat. returns a create review
    without a current character receives canAccept false with
    FOCUSED_CHARACTER_MIGRATION_NOT_READY despite a complete semantic review.
    This offline suite uses injected fake transport, not real provider execution.

evidence E2:
  |
    backend/src/services/semantic-authoring/adapters/character-v3.ts
    finalizeCharacterCandidate returns CharacterDefinitionV3 or a wrapped migration
    review candidate, not CharacterGenerationEnvelopeV3. orchestration.ts
    finalizeOrAsk marks this result ready_for_review. In character-focused-authoring.ts,
    persistFamilyResult stores result_json and marks the family attempt
    awaiting_owner_acceptance, but does not persist candidate_json with a profile.
    The generic semantic terminal result and complete activation envelope differ.

evidence E3:
  |
    backend/src/routes.ts focusedReviewAcceptance uses the migration trial flag and
    readCharacterFocusedMigrationActivationV3 for any awaiting semantic review.
    The latter explicitly throws FOCUSED_CHARACTER_MIGRATION_NOT_READY when
    row.mode is not migrate. Ordinary create is thus rejected by that branch.
    POST character-drafts/:id/chat only returns409 when structured.candidate exists
    and otherwise404; it has no focused ready-semantic candidate correction branch.

evidence E4:
  |
    character-authoring-candidate.ts assertCharacterCandidateReady requires a V3
    envelope, ready compiler compatibility, projection digest agreement and validated
    publicPresentation.claimValidation. Accepted ADR0011 public-profile section
    requires generated public profile and supported material claims before activation.
    character-v3-authoring-requirements-v5.md R18 requires complete safe final review
    and exact candidate/receipt binding; R21 forbids an independent budget reset.
    execution-policy.ts maxLlmCalls is8. The observed fixture consumed eight semantic
    calls, so blindly adding profile calls after terminal status is not a valid repair.

evidence E5:
  |
    Accepted ADR0030 D10 persistence clause, retained by foundation revision3 prior-contract disposition, states a different semantic result creates a
    new attempt. routes-structured-character-acceptance.test.ts currently requests
    cautious behavior via chat then expects the original attempt ID and confirms it.
    Updating that test must preserve successful correction and activation, using a
    new immutable attempt if supported, rather than simply expecting rejection.

evidence E6:
  |
    Competing explanations: a test-only outdated same-attempt expectation explains
    that identity mismatch but does not explain the independent create-review
    canAccept false result. A provider timeout does not explain a stored ready
    semantic candidate and the explicit mode guard. The source-producing historical
    change, prior review escape and full intended finalization architecture remain
    unknown. No paid run or production observation is evidence here.

decision D1 based_on P1, E1, E2, E3, E4, E6:
  |
    The demonstrated local mechanism is an incomplete create handoff: semantic
    readiness is promoted to family owner-ready status, while the consumer has only
    a migration activation reader and no complete create envelope. This produces
    the observed false create acceptance. Do not remove profile validation or treat
    semantic definition readiness as complete activation readiness.
    The historical root change and detection escape remain unknown; this conclusion
    is limited to the current offline code path, not actual provider reliability.

decision D2 based_on E1, E3, E5, E6:
  |
    The draft-correction failure has both a missing implementation branch and a
    same-attempt test expectation inconsistent with immutable semantic-result history.
    A rejection-only test edit would not fulfill successful owner correction.
    The exact successor command/source contract must be read before an implementation
    choice; no same-attempt mutation or fabricated active generation is selected here.

decision D3 based_on D1, D2, E4:
  |
    Next collect accepted focused-finalization and successor-source contracts and
    determine a complete envelope production path within the existing eight-call
    shared budget. Choose a typed required handoff only after that comparison.
    If this requires a changed budget or source/activation ownership contract, obtain
    an owner decision on a concrete design before dependent mutation. No code fix,
    broader quality conclusion, budget increase or new model calls are authorized by
    this reasoning artifact itself. Preserve all15 assertions' functional coverage.
